    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "2KI 1:17",
        "textualBasisJa": "So he died according to the LORD’s word which Elijah had spoken. Jehoram began to reign in his place in the second year of Jehoram the son of Jehoshaphat king of Judah, because he had no son."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 3:1",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now Jehoram the son of Ahab began to reign over Israel in Samaria in the eighteenth year of Jehoshaphat king of Judah, and reigned twelve years."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 3:7",
        "textualBasisJa": "He went and sent to Jehoshaphat the king of Judah, saying, “The king of Moab has rebelled against me. Will you go with me against Moab to battle?” He said, “I will go up. I am as you are, my people as your people, my horses as your horses.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 3:11",
        "textualBasisJa": "But Jehoshaphat said, “Isn’t there a prophet of the LORD here, that we may inquire of the LORD by him?” One of the king of Israel’s servants answered, “Elisha the son of Shaphat, who poured water on the hands of Elijah, is here.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 3:12",
        "textualBasisJa": "Jehoshaphat said, “The LORD’s word is with him.” So the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat and the king of Edom went down to him."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 3:14",
        "textualBasisJa": "Elisha said, “As the LORD of Armies lives, before whom I stand, surely, were it not that I respect the presence of Jehoshaphat the king of Judah, I would not look toward you, nor see you."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 8:16",
        "textualBasisJa": "In the fifth year of Joram the son of Ahab king of Israel, Jehoshaphat being king of Judah then, Jehoram the son of Jehoshaphat king of Judah began to reign."
      },
      {
        "ref": "2KI 12:18",
        "textualBasisJa": "Jehoash king of Judah took all the holy things that Jehoshaphat and Jehoram and Ahaziah, his fathers, kings of Judah, had dedicated, and his own holy things, and all the gold that was found in the treasures of the LORD’s house, and of the king’s house, and sent it to Hazael king of Syria; and he went away from Jerusalem."
      }
    ],
